      "writtenOn": "2021-11-23T18:00:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Might make more sens to specify that they must only support Digest SHA_2_512, since that is the digest they use. OTOH, that would require callers to actually specify a digest at the Java API layer, which is arguably redundant because there are no other options.\n\nPaul, WDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 321,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 321,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "a65f60be3c1e4c751f2a2397414bcbe61b206070",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9d58cad0_baadb7d8",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/IKeyMintDevice.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 321,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-23T19:40:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I started with that, but changed to Digest::NONE because it felt more natural in terms of what happens to the input data before it gets fed to the signature algorithm.  \n\n(It also falls out better internally in the implementation - the same AIDL Digest value gets mapped to the same BoringSSL EVP_MD digest.)",
      "parentUuid": "ea6dcfc1_8f3e40b2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 321,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 321,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "a65f60be3c1e4c751f2a2397414bcbe61b206070",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f72f636_3cb3e2a4",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/IKeyMintDevice.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 321,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060907
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-24T21:29:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there are arguments for both, but ISTR we decided to go for SHA_2_512 because if one day SHA3 (or SHA4) takes over the world and using anything else becomes unpopular, we might see a variant of Ed25519 specified that used a different hash function. In that case we\u0027ll end up with a wart if we don\u0027t specify SHA_2_512 here. OTOH it\u0027s very likely that this will never happen and we\u0027ll add extra complexity for nothing.",
      "parentUuid": "9d58cad0_baadb7d8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 321,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 321,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "a65f60be3c1e4c751f2a2397414bcbe61b206070",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b401663_9fdfd045",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/IKeyMintDevice.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 321,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-07T16:55:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We did originally decide to go for SHA_2_512, but it was going to lead to a bunch of special cases in the implementation -- all the OpenSSL entrypoints that allow  Ed25519 require an empty digest.  I wouldn\u0027t normally want implementation details to affect API design, but Digest::NONE does fit if you think of it as \"what happens to the data before it reaches the specified signature algorithm\".\n\nBut shout if you\u0027re vehemently against Digest::NONE and I can change it.",
      "parentUuid": "2f72f636_3cb3e2a4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 321,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 321,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "a65f60be3c1e4c751f2a2397414bcbe61b206070",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a07adb5_2cfb2b6f",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/IKeyMintDevice.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 321,
      "author": {
        "id": 1043663
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-09T23:08:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the day ever comes that there\u0027s an alternative to SHA-512, we can just specify that Digest::NONE or Digest::SHA_2_512 mean Digest::SHA_2_512, and Digest::FOO means Digest::FOO.  i.e. \"none\" defaults to SHA-512.  That would be ugly, but not horrible, and given the low probability I think it makes sense to optimize for the expected case.",
      "parentUuid": "9b401663_9fdfd045",
